<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiến quân ca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a>; published November <a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Tiến quân ca&quot; (&quot;The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> of the Marching Troops&quot;) is the national anthem of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Văn Cao wrote the words and composed the music of the march in 1944, drawing its words and title from his earlier work &quot;<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>&quot; (a former name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>). The words went through many changes in their early stages; Văn Cao revised several lines after many suggestions, toning down the fiercest of them.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Tiến quân ca</b>&quot; (&quot;The Song of the Marching Troops&quot;) is the national anthem of Vietnam.</blockquote><a href="/songs/tien-quan-ca">Tiến quân ca</a></li></ul></section>
